This read-only review initially captured twelve selected candidate/source/provenance files before author freeze. The captured before/after identities agree; this is not a final source freeze or behavioral acceptance. No candidate/application/original behavior has run in this review yet.

Fresh cases are selected independently from implementation inspection. The author test file was retained as a source snapshot but its case bodies were not read to design the fresh corpus. New original-engine comparisons will use owned synthetic files and authenticate the retained released executable before execution. Exact engine calls, source-helper calls, candidate actions and DOM-model groups must remain different counts; full workbench/native GUI executions remain zero.

Priorities are four-worker admission, disposal and awaited exit, deadline isolation, concurrent per-session refusal and output caps; scalar advancement on repeated zero-length hits, UTF-16 spans and CRLF/bare-CR treatment; option/read/Save publication guards and existing literal defaults. Unsupported syntax must fail explicitly. Unknown request fields retain the preceding ignored-field semantics and do not enable flags/globs/multiline; cancellation is workspace disposal, with no AbortSignal or UI cancel. These last limits were confirmed with the author before freeze.

The Close-tab/held-result-read hypothesis was shared with the author from the initial source pass. Author reproduction confirmed a negative before its fix and retained exact source/raw; it added a generation increment after accepted Close. This case must be labeled a shared source-review control, not a genuinely unseen independent case. It is also present by source in the prior production client and is separate from regex-engine novelty. The author additionally recorded its tab-selector fixture correction separately. This review has not executed that behavior yet.

No performance, memory benchmark, full-suite, original GUI, account operation, user4311 access or production write is authorized here. Author freeze/hash must arrive before fresh behavior execution. Every owned collector mistake and application counterexample will retain its exact source/raw/attempt identities.
